The exponential curve $y=2^x+1$ is shown. State the equation of its horizontal asymptote.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-3.3,xmax=3,ymin=-1,ymax=10,xtick={-3,-2,...,2},ytick={0,2,...,10},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,<->,domain=-3.3:3.1,samples=100] {exp(x*ln(2))+1};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
